# Target C — C86 lexicographic critical-flatness frontier

**LEVEL I STATUS: STILL OPEN.**

Full proof: [target_c_lexicographic_critical_flatness_2026-09-01.md](../../reports/target_c_lexicographic_critical_flatness_2026-09-01.md).

C63 and C65 together imply an exact finite statement that is stronger than their
original normalization use.

In the C65 lexicographically normalized hypothetical counterexample,

`C=C_*` and `H=H_*`.

Thus every active contact and every active diameter row is strong. For every
fixed-diameter critical velocity `v`, C63 gives an actual nearby feasible realization

`p(t)=p+t v+O(t^2)`.

Inactive pairs retain strict slack, so no new contact or diameter pair appears.
Primary contact minimality therefore prevents any old unit contact from opening.
After the contact graph is fixed, secondary diameter-pair minimality prevents any old
diameter pair from shortening. Consequently every C63 realization stays in the exact
active equality face:

`|p_i(t)-p_j(t)|=1` for every `ij in C`,

`|p_i(t)-p_j(t)|=D` for every `ij in H`.

## Exact-chain consequence

In the C80 chain-face branch,

`z=x_0,x_1,...,x_D=a`

is a literal `D`-edge unit-contact chain and `|z-a|=D`. Along every integrated critical
motion,

`D=|a(t)-z(t)| <= sum_j |x_j(t)-x_(j-1)(t)|=D`.

Equality in the triangle inequality forces all `D` unit chain edges to remain
parallel and co-oriented. Hence every critical velocity gives all chain edges one
common angular rate.

For the C80 ordered chain tracks `P={tau_1,...,tau_D}` this says

`v_tau1=...=v_tauD`

for every train-angle critical velocity.

Therefore the mean-zero chain-supported neutral space is zero:

`N_P={0}`.

C84 gives

`dim N_P=c(G_P)-1`,

so the prefix graph is necessarily connected.

## Combined C84 consequence

C84 already proves that the non-chain prefix interval multigraph carries a nowhere-zero
KKT circulation and has no bridges. Connectivity now gives

`|H_P|>=D+1`,

hence, including the chain bar,

`|H|>=D+2`.

Every chain cut is crossed by at least two non-chain diameter intervals with opposite
transverse KKT-flow signs.

## Effect on C85

C85's null-face half-mass theorem remains correct as a conditional statement, but its
hypothesis `N_P!=0` cannot occur in the C65 lexicographically normalized source.
The live exact-chain branch is therefore only the connected, bridgeless,
first-order high-capacity phase.

## Next target

Rule out a connected bridgeless prefix interval circulation on all `D+1` ordered chain
levels when its edges are actual planar diameter chords. Candidate inputs are the
straight-line diameter-thrackle property, shared-endpoint angular separation, near-disk
boundary curvature, and the extra train-separation cost of backward intervals.
